# EcrioniX — Commit + New Page Checklist

## After every edit session
- Always `git add` the relevant files, `git commit`, and `git push` to `origin` when the work is done.
- Do not leave finished edits uncommitted.
- Skip secrets / local-only files (`.env`, credentials, `.claude/settings.local.json` unless asked).
- Commit message style: short why-focused summary (e.g. `add light/dark theme across premium-course pages`).

## Every HTML page (new or edited)
1. **Google Analytics (GA4) on EVERY page** — ID `G-XXZS8C1FLY` immediately after `<head>` (AdSense may be above it). Never skip. Never use `G-TMJQ8CNQKL`.
```html
<script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-XXZS8C1FLY"></script>
<script>window.dataLayer=window.dataLayer||[];function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}gtag('js',new Date());gtag('config','G-XXZS8C1FLY');</script>
```
2. **AdSense** `ca-pub-6672302762343789` on public/content pages (articles, tools, problems, premium lessons). Skip only `/admin/` and empty redirect stubs. Never other ca-pub IDs.
3. **Open Graph** meta tags: `og:title`, `og:description`, `og:image`, `og:url`, `og:type`
4. Prefer `og:image` → `https://ecrionix.org/favicon1.png` unless a page-specific image exists
5. Visible breadcrumb nav (where site pattern uses it)
6. FAQPage JSON-LD + BreadcrumbList JSON-LD (public learning pages)
7. Copy buttons on code blocks + back-to-top when matching existing page patterns
8. Card on parent category index (if applicable)
9. IDX entry in root `index.html` (homepage search) when applicable
10. `sitemap.xml` entry in the **same commit** as the new page

## Premium / gated pages
- Still include GA4 + OG tags.
- Keep `noindex,follow` if that is the existing premium pattern.
- Include shared theme: early theme bootstrap + `/assets/theme-toggle.css` + `/assets/premium-theme.css` + `/assets/theme-toggle.js`, and a `#themeToggleSlot` in the navbar.
